Choose $n$ such that $T \le n$ (Bounded),
$$\begin{align*}
M_T & = M_0 + (M_1 - M_0) + (M_2 - M_1) + \dots + (M_T - M_{T-1}) \\
& = M_0 + \sum_{k=1}^n (M_k - M_{k-1}) 1_{T \ge k}
\end{align*}$$
so since $\{ T \ge k\} = \{ T \le k-1\}^c \in \mathcal{F}_{k-1}$, we have by the martingale property $$ \mathbb{E}((M_k - M_{k-1})1_{T \ge k}) = 0 \quad \forall k$$
